    "done_when": "Done when tests/test_a_tick_hands_its_freed_memory_back.py runs three ticks of a station whose tick is replaced by a stand-in, and asserts the release is made once after each tick, after the tick's own work, and that a tick that raises still releases. A second case on a platform without the call asserts the tick runs and nothing is called. An all_debug job runs the census harness ~/.config/reckon/crew/runs/r-20261115T101152745611-a-census-names-what-holds-the-stations-memory/census/run_census.sh at head and at base for six ticks each over the live crew home, read through its overlay and writing only a temporary store. The harness hardcodes its tree and revision, so the node first makes it take the revision and the log path as arguments: each arm builds its own worktree at its own revision and writes its own log, and each log opens with that revision. Each arm logs RSS and the tracemalloc peak after each tick: at head, RSS after the sixth tick is at most half of base's RSS after its sixth tick, and head's RSS after each tick is no more than 1.5 GB above that tick's tracemalloc peak. Negative control: the first case at base finds no release call. The test files importing the changed modules add no failure against base in matched arms run as an all_debug partition job, submitted with env -u SLURM_JOB_ID -u SLURM_JOBID sbatch and never on the fleet node. Each arm's log sits under the run directory, opens with its revision and literal command, and ends in EXIT= . The gate command is relative and literal ( PYTHONPATH=. .venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q followed by the test file), and names no worktree path. ruff check and ruff format --check add no finding on the staged paths.",
